PATCH 454: base-loss cluster in the c0e5-dispatched objtype-0x04 per-frame UPDATE method bab4 and its two
state sub-methods bae1/bb02.  di (object near offset) is threaded into each by the update walk (patch 243)
and the bab4 near-dispatch table @DGROUP:0x9c75 {bae1,bae0,bb02,bae0}, but Ghidra deref'd di as a HOST
pointer (*(param_1+off)) and, in bab4, dropped the DI arg + mis-based the near table onto a host offset.
Under ASLR these read/segfault at random host addresses (the crash the b26a-corrected trajectory now
reaches; masked by setarch -R where the garbage happens to be mapped) and, on wasm, read a DIFFERENT
address space -> divergence.  Rebased all three to the DGROUP model (g_mem+0x1c000+(u16)(di+off)); di
threaded into bab4's sub-dispatch.  ASM-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin @ 0xbab4/0xbae1/0xbb02.
bae0 (empty ret) needs no change.
